1
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:11,850
On a still day, a tree on the bank of a lake appears upside down in the water.

2
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:15,970
The top of the tree is 8 metres above the water line.

3
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:19,460
Where does the top of the tree appear in the reflection?

4
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:22,540
Pause the video and decide.

5
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:25,350
It appears 8 metres below the water line.

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,550
The water acts as a mirror line.

7
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:32,830
The reflection is the same distance from the line, on the other side.

8
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:36,230
Remember: a line such as x equals 2 is vertical.

9
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:39,610
A line such as y equals 1 is horizontal.

10
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:42,680
A reflection flips a shape over a mirror line.

11
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:47,510
Here, triangle A is reflected in the y axis, to give triangle B.

12
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:55,620
Each point of the image is the same distance from the mirror line as the object point, but on the opposite side.

13
00:00:55,670 --> 00:00:59,690
We measure that distance at right angles to the mirror line.

14
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:04,040
The image is congruent to the object, but it is flipped.

15
00:01:04,090 --> 00:01:07,350
Reflections in the axes follow a simple rule.

16
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,070
Reflect the point 3, 2 in the y axis.

17
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:13,930
The x coordinate changes sign: negative 3, 2.

18
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:15,980
Reflect 3, 2 in the x axis.

19
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:20,710
This time the y coordinate changes sign: 3, negative 2.

20
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,430
Your turn.

21
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,720
Reflect the point negative 5, 1 in the y axis.

22
00:01:24,770 --> 00:01:28,060
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:31,470
In the y axis, the x coordinate changes sign.

24
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,070
Negative 5 becomes 5.

25
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,980
The image is 5, 1.

26
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:37,980
For any other mirror line, count squares.

27
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:41,900
Reflect the point 3, 2 in the line x equals 1.

28
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:45,420
The point is 2 squares to the right of the line.

29
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:49,080
So the image is 2 squares to the left of the line.

30
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:51,390
1 minus 2 is negative 1.

31
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:53,350
The image is negative 1, 2.

32
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:56,300
The y coordinate does not change.

33
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:57,660
Here is the method.

34
00:01:57,710 --> 00:02:00,300
Step 1: find the mirror line.

35
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:05,760
Step 2: for each corner, count the squares to the line, at right angles.

36
00:02:05,810 --> 00:02:11,480
Step 3: count the same number on the other side, and mark the image corner.

37
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:16,770
Step 4: join the image corners, and check that the shape is flipped.

38
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:19,860
Reflect the triangle with corners 2, 1.

39
00:02:19,910 --> 00:02:20,650
Then 5, 1.

40
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:21,360
And 2, 4.

41
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:24,600
Use the y axis as the mirror line.

42
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:27,490
Change the sign of each x coordinate.

43
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:30,060
The corners become negative 2, 1.

44
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:31,540
Then negative 5, 1.

45
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:33,500
And negative 2, 4.

46
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:37,670
Reflect the point 6, 3 in the line x equals 2.

47
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:40,690
6 is 4 squares to the right of the line.

48
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:46,160
So go 4 squares to the left of the line: 2 minus 4 is negative 2.

49
00:02:46,210 --> 00:02:48,910
The image is negative 2, 3.

50
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:53,710
Reflect the point 4, negative 2 in the line y equals 1.

51
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:57,760
This mirror line is horizontal, so measure up and down.

52
00:02:57,810 --> 00:03:00,560
The point is 3 squares below the line.

53
00:03:00,610 --> 00:03:04,350
The image is 3 squares above: 1 plus 3 is 4.

54
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,730
The image is 4, 4.

55
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:07,470
Your turn.

56
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,840
Reflect the point 0, 3 in the line y equals 1.

57
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:14,220
Pause the video and try it.

58
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:17,130
The point is 2 squares above the line.

59
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:21,720
So the image is 2 squares below it: 1 minus 2 is negative 1.

60
00:03:21,770 --> 00:03:24,340
The image is 0, negative 1.

61
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:27,900
A point at negative 2, 4 has its image at 6, 4.

62
00:03:27,950 --> 00:03:30,050
Find the mirror line.

63
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:34,410
The mirror line is halfway between the point and its image.

64
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:37,770
Halfway between negative 2 and 6 is 2.

65
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:41,940
So the mirror line is the vertical line x equals 2.

66
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:45,280
Reflect the point 5, 6 in the line y equals 3.

67
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:46,950
Here is Kofi's working.

68
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,530
Which line goes wrong first?

69
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:50,650
Line 1 is wrong.

70
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:53,040
The line y equals 3 is horizontal.

71
00:03:53,090 --> 00:03:56,610
So measure up and down, not left and right.

72
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:59,420
The point is 3 squares above the line.

73
00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:03,010
The image is 3 squares below it, at 5, 0.

74
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:08,180
On the front of many ambulances, the word AMBULANCE is written back to front.

75
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:12,620
A driver ahead reads it the right way round in the mirror.

76
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:16,270
The Taj Mahal, in India, was built beside a long pool.

77
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:21,540
The pool reflects the whole building, upside down, like a mirror line.

78
00:04:21,590 --> 00:04:24,650
And your face in a mirror is a reflection too.

79
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:28,770
Raise your right hand, and the image raises its left.

80
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:29,990
One last question.

81
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,140
A point lies on the mirror line.

82
00:04:32,190 --> 00:04:36,790
When it is reflected, does it stay where it is, or move twice as far?

83
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:40,000
Pause the video and answer.

84
00:04:40,050 --> 00:04:41,440
It stays where it is.

85
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:47,030
Its distance from the mirror line is 0, so its image is in the same place.

86
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:51,600
To remember: a reflection flips a shape over a mirror line.

87
00:04:51,650 --> 00:04:57,840
Image points are the same distance from the line, on the other side, at right angles.

88
00:04:57,890 --> 00:04:59,790
In the x axis, y changes sign.

89
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:02,290
In the y axis, x changes sign.

90
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:05,510
Points on the mirror line do not move.

91
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:10,950
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.4 on Camday.
